-- title:
--   Intrinsic relative distance $d_{\mathrm{rel}}$
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal A=C^*(I_A,a_1,\dots,a_s)$ be generated by $N_A\times N_A$ matrices, let $\pi:\mathcal A\to B(H_B)$ be a unital $*$-homomorphism into the $N_B\times N_B$ matrices, and let $\tau_L(X)=\operatorname{Tr}X/N_L$ be the normalized traces. The **relative distance** of the marked, represented homomorphism is
--
--   $$d_{\mathrm{rel}}=\min\{t\in\mathbb N_0:\ \exists\,Y\in\mathcal F^A_t,\ \tau_B(\pi(Y))\neq\tau_A(Y)\},$$
--
--   with the empty minimum equal to $+\infty$ (Definition 4.1, eq. (45)).
--
--   A homomorphism transports polynomials but need not transport the physical traces; $d_{\mathrm{rel}}$ is the first word degree at which the two normalized traces disagree, and it controls the degree window in which the operator-state geometry is preserved.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The value lies in $\mathbb N\cup\{\infty\}$ (`ℕ∞`), as the infimum of the set of such $t$, so the empty set gives $+\infty$. $\tau_A$ is the normalized trace of the ambient matrix algebra evaluated on the underlying matrix of $Y$; $\tau_B$ is the normalized trace of $N_B\times N_B$ matrices.
-- source:
--   Shang, Stilck França, From Simple Sources to Quantum Advantage: Homomorphic Polynomial Transduction via Relative Decoding, arXiv:2609.35101 (held version, sha256 d2be7859…), Definition 4.1, eq. (45), p.18 (pdf_page 18)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_LIDT_MIPStarRE_Quantum_FiniteMatrix_NormalizedTrace
import Definitions.Def_RelDecoding_markedSpace

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace RelDecoding

open LIDT.MIPStarRE.Quantum

/-- The **intrinsic relative distance** of the marked, represented homomorphism
`π : A → B(H_B)`:
`d_rel = min{t ∈ ℕ₀ : ∃ Y ∈ 𝓕ᴬ_t, τ_B(π(Y)) ≠ τ_A(Y)}`, with the empty minimum equal to `+∞`.
Shang, Stilck França, *From Simple Sources to Quantum Advantage: Homomorphic Polynomial
Transduction via Relative Decoding*, arXiv:2609.35101 (held version, sha256 d2be7859…),
Definition 4.1, eq. (45), p.18.

**Formalization Note.** The value lies in `ℕ∞`, and the infimum of the empty set is `⊤ = +∞`, as
in the source. `τ_L = Tr / N_L` is `normalizedTrace`; `τ_A` is the normalized trace of the
ambient matrix algebra `Matrix nA nA ℂ` evaluated on the underlying matrix of `Y ∈ A`. The map
`π` is any unital ∗-homomorphism from `A = C∗(I_A, a)` into `Matrix nB nB ℂ`; its range is the
target algebra. -/
noncomputable def relDist {nA nB : Type*} [Fintype nA] [DecidableEq nA] [Fintype nB]
    [DecidableEq nB] {s : ℕ} (a : Fin s → Matrix nA nA ℂ)
    (π : genAlg a →⋆ₐ[ℂ] Matrix nB nB ℂ) : ℕ∞ :=
  sInf (((↑) : ℕ → ℕ∞) '' {t : ℕ | ∃ Y ∈ markedSpace a t,
    normalizedTrace (π Y) ≠ normalizedTrace (Y : Matrix nA nA ℂ)})

end RelDecoding


